  "notes": "{涵養|かんよう} implies gradual, patient nurturing over time, like water slowly soaking into the ground. The kanji {涵|かん} means \"to soak\" or \"to immerse.\"\n\nUsage:\n- {涵養|かんよう}する (to cultivate, nurture)\n- {涵養|かんよう}される (to be cultivated)\n\nCommonly used with:\n- {人材|じんざい} (human resources, talent)\n- {教養|きょうよう} (education, refinement)\n- {道徳心|どうとくしん} (moral sense)\n- {地下水|ちかすい} (groundwater - technical usage)\n\nNote: {水源|すいげん}{涵養|かんよう} (water source recharge) is an important environmental term.\n\nRelated words:\n- {養成|ようせい}する: to train, develop\n- {育成|いくせい}する: to nurture, cultivate\n- {醸成|じょうせい}する: to foster, brew",
